<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.13.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01103</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.13.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>b40ee9fb-ab8b-496c-b07b-39f4824d86ee</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="25e8169b-7e45-4c07-96a2-bcf904bf8b17" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q1a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="79dcc02b-722b-43fa-b175-5d7a3be32eb9" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="15">
    <problem>
      <para>The graph of function \(H\) shows the height, in meters, of a rocket \(t\) seconds after it was launched.<para><figure><media alt="Function on coordinate plane."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/45ceb267aeab7fc55ec544c03ba693d00323444a"/></media></figure></para>
          <para>Find \(H(0)\) in meters.</para>
          </para>
      <para> <emphasis> </emphasis></para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 15 meters, This is the height that the rocket was launched.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.13.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="401eedc3-c9dd-4ed4-8ce4-c33756bc18bb" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(0 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 4.5 \)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(0 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 35\\) &quot;, &quot;\\(0 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 4.5 \\)&quot;, &quot;\\(0 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 2\\) &quot;, &quot;\\(15 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 35\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which of the following describes the domain of this function?</para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(0 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 4.5\).; The domain includes all values from 0 to approximately 4.5, \(0 &amp;leq; x &amp;leq; 4.5\).</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.13.2-4.13.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="9d5fb4c0-2545-417f-bb2f-b1720b557e40" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(0 \leq \mathrm{y} \leq 35\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(0 \\leq \\mathrm{y} \\leq 35\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(0 \\leq \\mathrm{y} \\leq 4.5 \\)&quot;, &quot;\\(0\\leq \\mathrm{y} \\leq 2\\) &quot;, &quot;\\(15 \\leq \\mathrm{y} \\leq 35\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which of the following describes the range of this function?</para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(0\leq y\leq35\); The range includes all values from 0 to 35 meters, \(0\leq y\leq35\).</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.13.2-4.13.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="308650af-809d-41dc-99a1-98177f84e23c" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(2 \leq x \leq 7\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(0 \\leq x \\leq 9 \\)&quot;, &quot;\\(0 \\leq x \\leq 4\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(2 \\leq x \\leq 7\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(2 \\leq x \\leq 4\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which of the following describes the domain of the function graphed below?</para>
      <para><figure><media alt="Coordinate grid with wiggly graph. Horizontal axis by twos. Vertical axis by ones. Graphs starts around 2 comma 2 point 2 and ends around 7 comma 4."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/4e8936b6cc6c10289d3e2b1c42310598da4d0999"/></media></figure></para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(2≤x≤7\); The domain is all values from at least 2 to a maximum of 7, \(2≤x≤7\).</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.13.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="54e556fe-abbd-4d44-9fe1-5e2eae99e5db" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(2 \leq y \leq 4 \)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(2 \\leq y \\leq 4 \\)&quot;, &quot;\\(2 \\leq x \\leq 4\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(2 \\leq y \\leq 7\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(2 \\leq x \\leq 7\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which of the following describes the range of the graph below?</para>
      <para><figure><media alt="Coordinate grid with wiggly graph. Horizontal axis by twos. Vertical axis by ones. Graphs starts around 2 comma 2 point 2 and ends around 7 comma 4."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/4e8936b6cc6c10289d3e2b1c42310598da4d0999"/></media></figure></para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(2≤y≤4\); The range is all values from at least 2 to a maximum of 4, \(2≤y≤4\).</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.13.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="fbedf477-1e0e-4f57-85b8-283e720f9c26" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;-3&quot;, &quot;-2&quot;, &quot;2&quot;, &quot;4&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;-5&quot;, &quot;-3&quot;, &quot;-2&quot;, &quot;0&quot;, &quot;2&quot;, &quot;4&quot;, &quot;5&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para><emphasis>Select four</emphasis> of the values of the range for the function \(h\), graphed below.</para>
      <para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/56d0af3118e4ed206a7350ae234fec3ae6c71cb5"/></media></figure></para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! -3, -2, 2, 4</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.13.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="825d31c6-a7df-4505-a96d-d1ca287623d0" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(-5 \leq x \leq 5 \)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(-5 \\leq x \\leq 5 \\)&quot;, &quot;\\(-5 \\leq x \\leq 7\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(-5 \\leq y \\leq 5\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(-5 \\leq y \\leq 7\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which of the following is the domain of the function graphed below?</para>
      <para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/0223a9341fcd7ca2dc3e2ddd4b42c389dbad097e"/></media></figure></para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(-5≤x≤5\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.13.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="1cc90588-8a4b-4dd4-8ace-97732fc4dbe6" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(x \geq 2\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y \\geq 5 \\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x \\geq 5 \\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y \\geq 2 \\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x \\geq 2\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which of the following represents the domain of the function graphed below?</para>
      <para><figure><media alt="GRAPH OF A LINE FOR ALL X GREATER THAN OR EQUAL TO 2, WITH POINT SHOWN AT (2 5), AND PASSING THROUGH THE POINTS (3, 8) AND (5, 14)."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/a79cc63c6acdd168fd53633b75e6c1594d031438"/></media></figure></para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(x≥2\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.13.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q7-->
  <exercise data-content-id="86d3ccd0-8185-44eb-aa19-e218144f4a7b" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(y \geq 5 \)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y \\geq 5 \\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x \\geq 5 \\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y \\geq 2 \\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x \\geq 2\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which of the following represents the range of the function graphed below?</para>
      <para><figure><media alt="GRAPH OF A LINE FOR ALL X GREATER THAN OR EQUAL TO 2, WITH POINT SHOWN AT (2 5), AND PASSING THROUGH THE POINTS (3, 8) AND (5, 14)."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/a79cc63c6acdd168fd53633b75e6c1594d031438"/></media></figure></para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(y \geq 5 \)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.13.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> </div>
</div></section>
